{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scriptId": "pl-02-reverse-cp-sp-changed-price",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Reverse Cost Price, Selling Price and Changed Price",
    "description": "Work backward from a known profit or loss percentage, and solve questions where a different selling price changes loss into profit.",
    "teachingApproach": "Treat every known selling price as a percentage of one hidden C.P. Reverse that percentage first, then compare alternate selling prices. Develop the percentage-point gap shortcut only after showing why two outcomes share the same cost base.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach reverse percentage reasoning: if a sale at 20% loss gives an S.P., that S.P. is 80% of C.P.; if a sale at 25% gain gives an S.P., it is 125% of C.P. Use this to recover C.P., then compare alternate selling prices. Cover questions where a fixed rupee change turns a loss into a gain, where one selling price gives a known profit and another gives a different profit/loss, and where C.P. itself changes before resale. Emphasize the percentage-point gap method when two outcomes share the same C.P., and verify by reconstructing both selling prices."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn reverse cost price, selling price and changed price.\n\nA phone sells for ₹960 at a 20% loss. The cost price is hidden, but the words ‘20% loss’ tell us that ₹960 is exactly 80% of that hidden cost.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When the selling price is known but C.P. is missing, read the percentage backward. A sale at 20% loss means the S.P. is only 80% of the original cost.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If S.P. = ₹960 at 20% loss:\n80% of C.P. = 960\nC.P. = 960 × 100/80\n= ₹1200.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
